**EXERCISE 2.10.** Carry out the proof of Proposition 2.6; and in addition show that, if $f, g : D_0 \to D_1$ are two approximable mappings, there exists $h : D_0 \to D_1$ such that

$$
h(x) = f(x) \cap g(x)
$$

for all $x \in |D_0|$.

<!-- formalization -->

**Theorem (`exercise_2_10`).** The pointwise intersection of two approximable maps acts elementwise by intersection of filters.

*Proof.* This is the membership characterization of the pointwise meet. (The identity and composition laws of Proposition 2.6 are packaged separately.) ∎
